WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.803
(bright music)

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.900
- [Narrator] Nobody's born smart.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:09.723
We all start at zero.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:15.640
Can't talk, can't walk,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.063
certainly can't do algebra.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.480
Adding, reading, writing,

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.313
riding a bike,

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.270
nobody's good at anything at first.

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.480
There was a time when
Einstein couldn't count to 10

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.900
and Shakespeare had to learn his ABCs

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.283
just like the rest of us.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.553
Thankfully, we're born to learn.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:40.740
Slowly, surely, you stumble, slip, crawl,

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.563
fall, and fail, and fall,

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:47.580
frustrating, confusing,
trying, struggling,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.233
until one day, you walk.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:52.540
One foot in front of the other.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.590
One idea on top of the next.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:58.540
Each wrong answer making your
brain a little bit stronger.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:01.350
Failing is just another word for growing

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.260
and you keep going.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:05.350
This is learning.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:06.580
Knowing that you'll get it

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:08.950
even if you haven't gotten it yet.

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:11.000
Because the most
beautiful, complex concepts

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.770
in the whole universe
are built on basic ideas

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:16.503
that anyone anywhere can understand.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:20.720
Whoever you are, wherever you are,

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.320
you only have to know one thing,

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:26.253
you can learn anything.

